M<n> <area>: <imperative summary, 72 chars max>

WHAT:   One sentence. What changed, mechanically.
WHY:    1-3 sentences. The reason, tied to a requirement, a decision ID, or a
        measurement. Never "to improve things."
REVIEW: What the reviewer should check hardest, and what I am least sure about.
VERIFY: The exact commands run and their result.

# area: can | capture | ipc | store | analysis | supervisor | interface |
#       common | drivers | build | tests | tools | soak | docs
#
# One responsibility per commit, sized by what it is responsible for, not by
# line count (CLAUDE.md 7.3). The one-sentence test: if the summary needs "and",
# it is two commits. Past ~400 changed lines, say in WHY why it is indivisible.
# Banned: wip, fix, updates, misc, cleanup, changes, address feedback.
#
# Enable with:  git config commit.template .gitmessage
